 ## Overview
-Alpha-based Point Cleaning is a procedure to remove outlier points from a point cloud based on a threshold applied to their learned opacity (alpha) values [S1]. It solves the problem of noisy initial reconstructions (e.g., from COLMAP) or spurious points generated during training (e.g., from spawning mechanisms) by explicitly identifying points with low confidence [S1]. It is a child of Statistical Outlier Removal, specifically utilizing the alpha parameter rather than statistical distance [Parent](17819-statistical-outlier-removal.md).
+Alpha-based Point Cleaning is a procedure to remove outlier points from a point cloud based on a threshold applied to their learned opacity (alpha) values [S1]. It solves the problem of noisy initial reconstructions (e.g., from COLMAP) or spurious points generated during training (e.g., from spawning mechanisms) by explicitly identifying points with low confidence [S1]. It is a child of Statistical Outlier Removal [Parent](17819-statistical-outlier-removal.md), specifically utilizing a learned alpha threshold rather than statistical distance [S1].
 
